<!-- Content -->
<section class="bg-canvas px-6 md:px-8 pb-20">
  <div class="max-w-[640px] mx-auto">

    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Collator is built by R41. This policy explains, in plain language, what happens to your information when you use the app.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Our privacy philosophy</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Your data stays yours. Collator is designed so that we never see it in the first place. There are no accounts to create, no servers we operate, and nothing about your vault is ever shared or sold.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">What stays on your device</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Everything you add to Collator, documents, assets, policies, people, custody notes and succession details, is stored locally on your device. None of it is uploaded to a server we run, because we don't run one.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Backups</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      If you have device backups turned on, your vault may be included in your personal iCloud (iOS) or Google account (Android) backup, the same way your photos and messages are. That backup is encrypted and controlled entirely by Apple or Google under your own account. We have no access to it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">What we collect, and what we don't</h2>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 my-6">
      <div class="bg-card border border-hair rounded-[20px] p-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-[.875rem] text-ink mb-3">Collator stores, on your device</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2.5">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[.9375rem] text-dim">
            <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-inset text-marigold-deep flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              {% icon "check", "w-3 h-3" %}
            </span>
            Documents, notes and files you add, including any photos or scans
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[.9375rem] text-dim">
            <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-inset text-marigold-deep flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              {% icon "check", "w-3 h-3" %}
            </span>
            Records about assets, policies, accounts and people you choose to track
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[.9375rem] text-dim">
            <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-inset text-marigold-deep flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              {% icon "check", "w-3 h-3" %}
            </span>
            Custody notes, where physical originals are kept
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[.9375rem] text-dim">
            <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-inset text-marigold-deep flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              {% icon "check", "w-3 h-3" %}
            </span>
            App settings and preferences, such as theme and lock method
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-card border border-hair rounded-[20px] p-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-[.875rem] text-ink mb-3">We never collect</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2.5">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[.9375rem] text-dim">
            <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-inset text-muted flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              {% icon "x", "w-3 h-3" %}
            </span>
            Your name, email address or phone number
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[.9375rem] text-dim">
            <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-inset text-muted flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              {% icon "x", "w-3 h-3" %}
            </span>
            Your location for tracking, profiling or advertising
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[.9375rem] text-dim">
            <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-inset text-muted flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              {% icon "x", "w-3 h-3" %}
            </span>
            Device identifiers or advertising IDs
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[.9375rem] text-dim">
            <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-inset text-muted flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              {% icon "x", "w-3 h-3" %}
            </span>
            Usage analytics or app activity
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[.9375rem] text-dim">
            <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-inset text-muted flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              {% icon "x", "w-3 h-3" %}
            </span>
            Contacts, calendar or photos beyond what you choose to attach
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Collator does not run analytics, advertising or crash-tracking software of any kind. There is nothing to opt out of, because nothing is being watched.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Permissions the app may ask for</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      If you photograph or scan a document, the image is stored only on your device, and in your personal backup if you have one enabled. We never receive it.
    </p>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      If you turn on an app lock, Face ID, Touch ID or fingerprint authentication is handled entirely by your device's operating system. Collator never receives or stores biometric data.
    </p>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      If you set a reminder for a renewal or expiry date, it is scheduled using your device's own notification system. Reminder data never leaves your device.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Maps and address lookup</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      When you search for an address while saving a document's location or a custody note, Collator sends the text you type to Google's Maps and Places service so it can return matching places, and map tiles are loaded from a maps provider. Google processes these requests under its own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-marigold-deep underline-offset-4 hover:underline">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Collator sends only the search text and map view needed to show results. It does not attach your name or any identifier, and nothing else from your vault is included. If you never use address search, no map or location data is ever sent.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Purchases</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Purchases are processed directly by the Apple App Store or Google Play. To check whether your purchase has unlocked the app's paid features, Collator uses <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" class="text-marigold-deep underline-offset-4 hover:underline">RevenueCat</a>. RevenueCat receives a random, app-generated identifier and the purchase receipt from the store, never your name, email address or payment details.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Your control over your data</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Because everything lives on your device, you can view, edit, export or delete it at any time from within the app. Uninstalling Collator removes its local data from your device. Whether a copy remains in your personal device backup is controlled by your iCloud or Google account settings, not by us.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Children's privacy</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Collator is designed for managing personal, financial and legal records and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect information from children, and as explained above, we do not collect personal information from anyone.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">International users</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Collator can be used anywhere. Because your data is stored on your device rather than on our servers, there is no cross-border transfer of your information by us.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      If this policy changes, we'll update the date at the top of this page. Continuing to use Collator after a change means you accept the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Contact us</h2>
    <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed mb-8">
      Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}" class="text-marigold-deep underline-offset-4 hover:underline">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>.
    </p>

